# The image must stay small and the build context must never carry the dataset.
#
# The FSG output is ~2.1 GB behind Git LFS and is *mounted*, never baked. It already
# sits outside this build context (the context is `llm_insights/`, the dataset is its
# sibling `one_way_fsg_model/`), so it cannot be copied in even by accident. The lines
# below cover the things that are inside the context and should not travel.

# Virtualenvs. The image builds its own; a host venv holds macOS wheels that would not
# run on linux anyway, and .venv/ alone is several hundred MB of build context.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Caches and build artifacts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.DS_Store

# Generated output: reports, cards, briefings, scratch runs, precomputed surfaces.
# One file is deliberately kept -- the recorded transcript the `smoke` entrypoint
# replays, which is what lets the container prove itself with no model and no network.
data/
!data/demo_transcript.json

# Working notes. They change constantly and would bust the layer cache for nothing.
TASKS/
